From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caner Altinbasak <cal@brightsign.biz>
Date: Wed, 29 Jan 2025 15:23:05 +0000
Subject: fix(nexus): Fix window focus management for VK OS-17597

Virtual keyboard should receive mouse events,
but it shouldn't take the focus. It will always
be the last window created, and it should only
get events when it is visible. Based on these
assumptions I've made following changes:

Converted window idMap to std::map to be able
to use reverse iterator. We start from top
of the window stack and go towards the bottom.

If a window can handle the event, the propagation
stops.

Virtual keyboard handles the mouse events, when
it is visible. If virtual keyboard is not visible,
the next window under the cursor receives the event.

